-- The rule of `Reject.ConstGeneric.yana` the default stage does not refuse yet: a const parameter
-- reused as a value parameter's name. It accepts the declaration; only a call then fails, with
-- "no argument decides what n is". Move it back when it does.

-- §1.6: a const parameter and an ordinary parameter of the same name are two things called `n` in
-- one signature, reported at the declaration rather than resolved by shadowing.
fn (n: Int) twice(n: Int) -> Int = n

fn main() -> Int = 0
